WEBVTT

00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:10.759
<v David Whitfield>Morning, everyone. Friday the twenty-second. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the silent film again?</v>

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.829
<v Priya Raman>We can hear you. Um, more importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office.</v>

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.960
<v Jamie Brennan>That's the clearest bit of communication we've had all week.</v>

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:28.339
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the charity bake sale on Friday — today. Dangerous day to have forgotten your breakfast.</v>

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:32.200
<v Tomasz Nowak>Forgotten? That's a deliberate strategy.</v>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.579
<v Priya Raman>The cake's already been cut, before anyone thinks I'm organising something here.</v>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.149
<v David Whitfield>Right, excellent. Cake situation understood. Finished stuff first?</v>

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.869
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I signed off the inspection on the wrapper on Tuesday. That's closed, nothing new off that.</v>

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.109
<v David Whitfield>Cheers, Grace. That can stay in the done pile.</v>

00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:00.880
<v Callum Reid>I finished the repair on the Palletiser last night as well. That repair's complete.</v>

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:08.359
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, although there's the jam on the palletizer to talk about. Not saying your finished repair is still open.</v>

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:12.719
<v Callum Reid>No, exactly. The repair from last night is done. Separate conversation.</v>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:21.010
<v Priya Raman>And I finished the repair on the line 2 robot last night. That's done too, not another one for today.</v>

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.680
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. Any observations before we get into the actual jobs?</v>

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:34.670
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I saw the pressure on the line one HPU dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own. Just an observation.</v>

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:38.579
<v David Whitfield>Right, so that's not a new investigation being allocated here.</v>

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:44.709
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Correct. It recovered on its own; just giving you the picture.</v>

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:53.349
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I can't get to the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller until production gives us a window. Still blocked.</v>

00:01:55.269 --> 00:01:59.120
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, there's no window confirmed for that. Can't pretend there is.</v>

00:02:01.019 --> 00:02:03.469
<v David Whitfield>Understood. Blocked, not a commitment for today.</v>

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:12.979
<v Priya Raman>Oh, and we were going to replace the belt on the line 3 barrel but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:18.219
<v Tomasz Nowak>The belt, yeah. Bearings are a separate thing, though?</v>

00:02:19.789 --> 00:02:27.139
<v David Whitfield>They are. Tom, can you grease and check the bearings on the line 3 barrel today? No belt replacement in that.</v>

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:35.400
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll grease and check the bearings on the line 3 barrel today. Just the bearings, understood.</v>

00:02:37.509 --> 00:02:38.909
<v David Whitfield>Thanks, Tom. That's agreed.</v>

00:02:41.379 --> 00:02:51.530
<v Callum Reid>Right, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Line 3 Chiller by the end of the week. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:57.860
<v David Whitfield>Thanks, Callum. By the end of the week, and first for you because it's holding production up.</v>

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:02.729
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. I'll take the permit to work and isolation, yes.</v>

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:10.060
<v Grace Liu>I'll replace the seals on the boiler feed pump on Friday. It's urgent, that one.</v>

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:15.979
<v David Whitfield>Okay, Grace. The seals on the boiler feed pump, on Friday — today — and urgent.</v>

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.620
<v Grace Liu>Yes, today. I'll take that.</v>

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:24.080
<v Jamie Brennan>Right. Definitely not everything in the 'when you fancy it' category, then.</v>

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:31.229
<v David Whitfield>Definitely not. Olumide Adeyemi, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:39.699
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer. I'll take it as top priority.</v>

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:45.620
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, talking over you — just keeping that distinct from the repair I finished last night.</v>

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:51.819
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, understood. I'm taking the jam and sensor check, not reopening your repair.</v>

00:03:52.419 --> 00:03:54.520
<v David Whitfield>Good. Top priority for that, agreed.</v>

00:03:55.389 --> 00:04:00.639
<v Priya Raman>On the buying side, I'll chase the purchase order for the water system this morning.</v>

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:05.550
<v Jamie Brennan>Is that an urgent chase, or just whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:12.080
<v Priya Raman>Whenever you get a chance sort of priority. I'll fit the chase in this morning, though.</v>

00:04:14.509 --> 00:04:20.459
<v David Whitfield>Okay, PR. Purchase order for the water system, this morning, whenever you get a chance. Got it.</v>

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.850
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers. That's the chase covered, then.</v>

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:32.899
<v Grace Liu>I've got the pressure one as well. I'll investigate the pressure drop on the Boiler Feedwater Pump by the 28th. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:40.279
<v David Whitfield>Just so I've got that straight, normal priority for the investigation, rather than the urgency on the seals?</v>

00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:46.959
<v Grace Liu>Yes. Normal priority for the pressure-drop investigation, by the 28th. The seal replacement is the urgent one.</v>

00:04:47.389 --> 00:04:49.839
<v David Whitfield>Thanks, Grace. Separate entries, separate priorities. Clear.</v>

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:54.860
<v Priya Raman>And I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team after lunch.</v>

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:03.610
<v David Whitfield>Thanks, PR. Whenever you get a chance after lunch — that doesn't need to jump ahead of the urgent stuff.</v>

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:09.149
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll organise it after lunch, whenever I get a chance. That's fine.</v>

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.810
<v Tomasz Nowak>Toolbox talk versus cake. Tough audience you've got there.</v>

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:20.279
<v Priya Raman>It's organising the talk, not a promise of cake with every safety message.</v>

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.269
<v David Whitfield>And I'll send the shift handover report round Monday. No rush on that one.</v>

00:05:29.379 --> 00:05:33.579
<v Callum Reid>Monday for the report, Davey? Not expecting it in amongst all this?</v>

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.129
<v David Whitfield>That's right. I'll send it round Monday, no rush.</v>

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:43.769
<v Jamie Brennan>Good. For a second I thought we'd somehow got to Monday already.</v>

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.870
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Don't do that. I've only just mentally arrived at Friday's bake sale.</v>

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.819
<v David Whitfield>Right. And nothing's quietly slipped in from the blocked or cancelled list?</v>

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:02.800
<v Tomasz Nowak>No. Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller is still blocked on access. Not down as something I'm doing today.</v>

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:10.629
<v Priya Raman>And the belt replacement on the line 3 barrel is still pushed to next month. Not part of today's bearings job.</v>

00:06:12.329 --> 00:06:15.480
<v David Whitfield>Good. Any crossed wires on what we've actually agreed?</v>

00:06:17.899 --> 00:06:22.449
<v Grace Liu>No, all clear from me. Urgent seals and normal-priority pressure investigation, kept separate.</v>

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:28.470
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. I'll let you get off Teams before the cake discussion starts again.</v>
